1
00:00:00,065 --> 00:00:01,589
November 2008.

2
00:00:02,005 --> 00:00:04,049
A doctor from Chicago checks into the

3
00:00:04,050 --> 00:00:06,576
Taj Mahal Palace Hotel in Mumbai.

4
00:00:06,992 --> 00:00:09,727
He is there on business — his immigration

5
00:00:09,740 --> 00:00:12,057
consultancy has an office in the city.

6
00:00:13,347 --> 00:00:16,147
About eleven days later, gunmen will be

7
00:00:16,160 --> 00:00:17,852
walking the same corridors.

8
00:00:19,026 --> 00:00:20,510
He never fires a shot.

9
00:00:20,914 --> 00:00:22,542
He never plans a target.

10
00:00:22,958 --> 00:00:25,836
What he supplies is rarer: a cover story.

11
00:00:27,011 --> 00:00:29,798
Three years later, an American jury clears

12
00:00:29,811 --> 00:00:32,154
him of helping plan the Mumbai attacks.

13
00:00:33,401 --> 00:00:33,896
Cleared.

14
00:00:34,313 --> 00:00:36,943
And fourteen years after that, India flies

15
00:00:36,956 --> 00:00:38,896
him to Delhi to stand trial for them

16
00:00:38,909 --> 00:00:39,404
anyway.

17
00:00:39,820 --> 00:00:42,125
How can a man be acquitted of an attack —

18
00:00:42,320 --> 00:00:44,573
and still be sent home to answer for it?

